          ],
          "content": "(i) How many ants are there for every human in the world?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.385,
            0.846,
            0.421
          ],
          "content": "(ii) If a flock of starlings contains 10,000 birds, how many flocks could there be in the world?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.421,
            0.846,
            0.458
          ],
          "content": "(iii) If each tree had about 10<sup>4</sup> leaves, find the total number of leaves on all the trees in the world."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.458,
            0.847,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": "(iv) If you stacked sheets of paper on top of each other, how many would you need to reach the Moon?"
